      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay here is my proposal which you/michael can discuss which approach (yours vs mind) you like better. I\u0027m fine with either.\n\n1) similar to what we do in `VulkanWindowContext`, update the Ganesh GL mac version to call flush on the main surface, https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/tools/window/mac/GaneshGLWindowContext_mac.mm;l\u003d122.\n\n2) In the flush call set SkSurfaces::BackendSurfaceAccess::kPresent.\n\n3) Have GrGLGpu.cpp override `prepareSurfacesForBackendAccessAndStateUpdates`. We\u0027ll want asserts here that the surface wraps FBO0 and no mutable state.\n\n4) In that call if access is kPresent and we\u0027ve enable the workaround, `bindDefaultFramebufferOnPresent`, then we\u0027ll do a bind call.",
